<title>USA: Xetel says to reduce workforce seven pct.</title>
<headline>Xetel says to reduce workforce seven pct.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN, Texas 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>XeTel Corp said on Monday it cut its workforce by approximately 35 employees, or 7 percent, after two major customers cancelled orders.</p>
<p>This action, together with other cost saving measures were necessary to bring expenses more in line with revenues, the company said.</p>
<p>It could not immediately be determined whether the company is taking a charge against earnings from thse job cuts.</p>
<p>As of Sept. 30, 1996 the company employed approximately 515 employees.</p>
